(* Candidate semantic producer interfaces only, NOT a callee simulation.
   No initialized-value obligation is imposed on fresh ALLOCA capacity. *)
Theory bodyPtrStructLitInitialization
Ancestors bodyPtrStructLitReturnAudit bodyPtrDefs valueEncoding valueEncodingProps
  valueEncodingProofs ptrDiscipline pred_set list

Theorem structlit_robust_representation_join:
  !c tv v1 v2 p1 p2 tn1 tn2 mem1 mem2.
    (!m. mem_agree_outside tn1 mem1 m ==> val_in_memory tv v1 p1 m) /\
    (!m. mem_agree_outside tn2 mem2 m ==> val_in_memory tv v2 p2 m) ==>
    !m. mem_agree_outside (if c then tn1 else tn2)
           (if c then mem1 else mem2) m ==>
        val_in_memory tv (if c then v1 else v2) (if c then p1 else p2) m
Proof
  Cases_on `c` >> simp[]
QED

Theorem structlit_return_robust_representation_boundary:
  !tn mem0.
    mem_word_at 64 mem0 = 0w /\ mem_word_at 160 mem0 = 0w /\
    (!j. j < 32 ==> j + 64 NOTIN tn /\ j + 160 NOTIN tn) ==>
    !mem. mem_agree_outside tn mem0 mem ==>
      val_in_memory
        (TupleTV [BaseTV (BytesT (Dynamic 33));
                  ArrayTV (BaseTV BoolT) (Dynamic 1)])
        (ArrayV (TupleV [BytesV []; ArrayV (DynArrayV [])])) 64 mem
Proof
  rpt gen_tac >> strip_tac >> rpt gen_tac >> disch_tac >>
  rewrite_tac[structlit_return_representation_test] >>
  `!a. a = 64 \/ a = 160 ==> mem_word_at a mem0 = mem_word_at a mem` by
    (rpt strip_tac >>
     simp[mem_word_at_def, GSYM mem_bytes_at_def] >>
     AP_TERM_TAC >> irule LIST_EQ >> simp[EL_mem_bytes_at] >>
     rpt strip_tac >>
     `a + x NOTIN tn` by (gvs[] >> metis_tac[arithmeticTheory.ADD_COMM]) >>
     `mem_bytes_at (a+x) 1 mem0 = mem_bytes_at (a+x) 1 mem` by
       (fs[mem_agree_outside_def] >> first_x_assum irule >> simp[]) >>
     pop_assum mp_tac >> simp[LIST_EQ_REWRITE, EL_mem_bytes_at]) >>
  metis_tac[]
QED

(* C1.9 candidate interface / remaining cases (not asserted as a theorem).

   At a statement boundary the existing ghost_inv already supplies the
   desired initialized-local relation, at entry.type rather than an AST
   annotation (bodyPtrDefs:80-92). A precise intermediate candidate is

     ghost_inv d cenv cx es G tn s /\
     (!tv v p. (tv,v,p) IN C ==>
       !mem. mem_agree_outside tn.t_mem s.vs_memory mem ==>
             val_in_memory tv v p mem)

   C contains only COMPLETED temporary fields/values. Fresh allocation and
   uninitialized return capacity add nothing to C. ghost_inv's local part
   quantifies lookup_scopes name es.scopes = SOME entry and
   FLOOKUP cenv.ce_vars name = SOME (PtrVar (Var p) sz), then ptr_covers and
   robust entry.type/entry.value representation at lookup_var p's address.
   return_buf_ptr asks for coverage, not a preinitialized return value.
   Thus no new global definition or replacement semantics is needed here.

   Return continuation strengthens this with
     !mem. mem_agree_outside tn.t_mem s.vs_memory mem ==>
           val_in_memory rtv v dst mem
   where evaluate_type (get_tenv cx) declared_return_type = SOME rtv.
   The fixture-specific boundary above validates this *only* given both
   zero words and their cleanliness. For general v the existing
   robust_val_in_memory_copy_transport also requires val_wf rtv v,
   val_footprint rtv v <= n, exact copied bytes and pointwise taint transport.
   It does not generate robustness of the expression at rtv.

   Join: structlit_robust_representation_join checks branch-specific
   memory, taint, address and value. A joined obligation can be retained
   only if it holds in BOTH branch invariant sets (C1 INTER C2); no
   obligation on an uncompleted field is manufactured at the join.

   Recursion is NOT plain AST size or arbitrary target fuel. Source
   evaluate_ind is generated by the measure in vyperInterpreter:1783-1796:
     expression rank = 4 * expr_bound (remcode cx) e
     statement-list rank = 4 * stmts_bound (remcode cx) ss.
   The candidate recursive hypothesis is the SAME robust simulation
   relation for every evaluator configuration of strictly smaller rank,
   quantified over its legal body_inv-linked context and initial ghost.
   For internal calls, bodySimCallCases:68-100 gives a body IH at cxf after
   push_function (src_id_opt,fn) env cx, conditional on the complete source
   call prefix. remcode filters the active cx.stk; termination proof
   vyperInterpreter:1819-1845 unfolds push_function/remcode and removes the
   called entry. This supplies the callee-body smaller rank and handles
   nested calls without assuming unrelated function simulations.

   Required linkage is body_inv tops ctx cenv cx, hence actual lowering of
   tops to ctx and ce_func_* metadata from those tops. Callee lookup must
   be that compiled function with the same declared-return map. Existing
   fixture supplies none of this linkage (E0024).

   Outstanding preservation constructors: bind_arguments/parameter copies,
   declarations and local assignments (new initialized bindings), stores
   to places and aggregate fields, sequential blocks, If/IfExp joins,
   loops and mutation, return expression/copy, and nested internal calls
   (argument/default evaluation, prologue bindings, body, result copy).
   StructLit is itself an aggregate-expression constructor in that mutual
   induction. Proving this producer by assuming the present frozen
   structlit case would be circular. A simultaneous robust strengthening
   would need a new scoped plan covering every one of those cases.
   In addition, the pointer-run half still meets E0023's literal-frame
   access obstruction at lo=0; these semantic interfaces do NOT fix it.
*)
